1
00:00:00,900 --> 00:00:04,033
From lesson observation to a plan for every teacher.

2
00:00:04,033 --> 00:00:09,254
Here is what the system does today, and where staff voice fits into it.

3
00:00:09,874 --> 00:00:12,853
Every R3 lesson observation is filed on one form.

4
00:00:12,853 --> 00:00:18,810
In the June round that was a hundred and sixty eight submissions, because inspectors observed in pairs.

5
00:00:18,810 --> 00:00:24,767
The system resolves those into a hundred and ten distinct lessons, across a hundred and four teachers.

6
00:00:24,767 --> 00:00:28,076
Nothing is typed twice, and nothing is counted twice.

7
00:00:28,696 --> 00:00:30,573
Those lessons land on one board.

8
00:00:30,573 --> 00:00:33,076
Leadership sees the round at a glance.

9
00:00:33,076 --> 00:00:34,327
How many lessons.

10
00:00:34,327 --> 00:00:35,579
How many teachers.

11
00:00:35,579 --> 00:00:38,707
Where the judgements sit on the six point scale.

12
00:00:38,707 --> 00:00:41,523
What is working, and where to focus next.

13
00:00:42,143 --> 00:00:44,868
Every claim on that board carries a number.

14
00:00:44,868 --> 00:00:52,362
Open it, and you get the lessons behind the claim, the inspector's own words, and a link to the locked record.

15
00:00:52,362 --> 00:00:57,131
More than six hundred of those references sit behind the June round alone.

16
00:00:57,131 --> 00:00:59,515
No statement stands on its own.

17
00:01:00,135 --> 00:01:02,828
From there the loop runs in four steps.

18
00:01:02,828 --> 00:01:04,510
The observation is filed.

19
00:01:04,510 --> 00:01:06,530
The teacher is given feedback.

20
00:01:06,530 --> 00:01:12,252
The observer receives an analysis and a suggested coaching plan, which they approve, edit, or rewrite.

21
00:01:12,252 --> 00:01:18,310
And the teacher receives that plan, with every suggestion referenced back to our own Student Progress Rubric.

22
00:01:18,930 --> 00:01:21,287
This is what the observer actually receives.

23
00:01:21,287 --> 00:01:25,1000
This teacher is Acceptable on progress in lessons, and the plan targets Good.

24
00:01:25,1000 --> 00:01:34,753
It carries the rubric line for that level, one concrete move, what to look for in the next lesson, and where the technique comes from.

25
00:01:34,753 --> 00:01:38,456
The observer approves it, edits it, or writes their own.

26
00:01:39,076 --> 00:01:42,405
What the loop does not hear yet is the teacher.

27
00:01:42,405 --> 00:01:45,068
We capture how a session was rated.

28
00:01:45,068 --> 00:01:54,055
We do not capture what the teacher made of it, what they expect to struggle with, or what they intend to do differently on Monday morning.

29
00:01:54,675 --> 00:01:56,020
So, the first addition.

30
00:01:56,020 --> 00:01:59,048
An evaluation of the professional learning session itself.

31
00:01:59,048 --> 00:02:01,403
Short, and completed by the teacher.

32
00:02:01,403 --> 00:02:08,130
It sits before the coaching plan is drafted, so that the observer, and the analysis, both see it first.

33
00:02:08,750 --> 00:02:09,716
The second addition.

34
00:02:09,716 --> 00:02:11,970
A reflection, and an action plan.

35
00:02:11,970 --> 00:02:12,936
Six things.

36
00:02:12,936 --> 00:02:15,512
What the teacher took from the session.

37
00:02:15,512 --> 00:02:18,410
The challenges they expect when they apply it.

38
00:02:18,410 --> 00:02:21,309
Their own ideas for getting past those challenges.

39
00:02:21,309 --> 00:02:24,207
How they will use it in their classroom.

40
00:02:24,207 --> 00:02:26,783
What they need from their middle leader.

41
00:02:26,783 --> 00:02:31,291
And what they expect to change in student learning, and over what timeframe.

42
00:02:31,911 --> 00:02:34,745
Each of those answers meets something ready made.

43
00:02:34,745 --> 00:02:43,601
Five coaching strategies, with worked examples, mapped point by point onto the Student Progress Rubric, and built on our own Teaching and Learning Agenda.

44
00:02:43,601 --> 00:02:47,497
The observer and the analysis draw from the same shelf.

45
00:02:47,497 --> 00:02:54,228
The teacher gets something that is recognisably ours, and it takes the observer minutes rather than an evening.

46
00:02:54,848 --> 00:02:58,925
Then the staff responses get the same treatment as the observation data.

47
00:02:58,925 --> 00:03:03,002
Themes across the school, rather than a folder of individual replies.

48
00:03:03,002 --> 00:03:05,380
Where support is being asked for.

49
00:03:05,380 --> 00:03:07,418
Which challenges repeat, and where.

50
00:03:07,418 --> 00:03:11,835
All of it carrying its references, exactly as the observation claims do.

51
00:03:12,455 --> 00:03:15,432
Middle leaders see their own team, and nobody else's.

52
00:03:15,432 --> 00:03:17,748
Not a report to read through.

53
00:03:17,748 --> 00:03:23,702
A starting point for a coaching conversation, with the teacher's own words already in front of them.

54
00:03:24,322 --> 00:03:28,253
Which gives every teacher the same thing the observation already gives them.

55
00:03:28,253 --> 00:03:35,133
A plan of their own, built from their own lesson and their own words, in language the school already uses.

56
00:03:35,753 --> 00:03:37,444
The two forms are new.

57
00:03:37,444 --> 00:03:39,135
The architecture is not.

58
00:03:39,135 --> 00:03:45,560
Same intake, same evidence rules, same dashboard, same privacy layer, with the data staying in our own database.

59
00:03:45,560 --> 00:03:48,603
Student surveys run on the same rails next.
